{"archetypes":[{"name":"cross-ref","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan cites dozens of specific line numbers across six files; stale references would cause the implementer to target wrong code or assert a contract that does not exist.","prompt_body":"Verify every line-number citation the plan makes against the actual current file content: review-core.sh lines 453-514 and 596, dispatch-plan-review-panel.sh lines 90, 91, 97, 98, 116, 117, 123, 124 (where fallback_group is claimed already emitted), test-aggregate-findings.sh lines 1332 and 1386, aggregate-findings.md line 26, and test-review-core.sh lines 337-354. For each cited range check whether the described code is actually present at that location in the current checked-in files. Specifically confirm the plan's claim that fallback_group is already emitted in dispatch-plan-review-panel.sh at those eight lines per commit 2fc03694, and confirm the stub at test-review-core.sh:337-354 actually emits AGGREGATED=true, INPUT_COUNT=2, MERGED_COUNT=0, and REASON=ok as assumed. Flag any mismatch between the plan description and observed file content as a plan defect that would cause the implementer to target or test the wrong location. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"shell-extraction","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Item B's 62-line function extraction is the highest-risk change in the plan; the plan flags outer-variable scope as the top failure mode but only gives a high-level mitigation with no enumeration of which variables are actually read or written in the block.","prompt_body":"Read the zero-findings early-exit block in review-core.sh at the lines the plan identifies (approximately 453-514) and enumerate every outer-scope variable that block reads or writes. Verify that each such variable would remain accessible in a regular bash function (not a subshell) defined in the same script, or flag any that require explicit argument passthrough to avoid unbound-variable errors under set -euo pipefail. Cross-check the plan's variable list (panel_manifest, collector_results_file, not_substantive_slots, scout_status, dynamic_slots, static_slot_count, panel_mode, panel_shape, ROUND_NUM, MODE, SESSION_ENV_PATH, IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR, CURSOR_AVAILABLE, CODEX_AVAILABLE, TALLY_VOTES_SH, flush_round_log) against what the block actually references — note any variables the plan lists that the block does not use, and any the block uses that the plan omits, since both are evidence of a plan drafted from an inaccurate snapshot. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
